      "abstract": "Particle yield differences $\\mathrm{R^{asym}}-\\mathrm{R^{sym}}$ as a function of $\\Delta\\eta^{\\mathrm{ch}, \\mathrm{jet}_{1}}$ for central $(0-30\\%)$ PbPb collisions. The results correspond to the charged-particle transverse momentum range $1 < p^{\\mathrm{ch}}_{\\mathrm{T}} < 2$ GeV for $\\mathrm{R^{asym}}$ with $\\Delta\\eta^{\\mathrm{jet}_{1}, \\mathrm{jet}_{2}} \\in (0.5, 1.0)$, $\\Delta\\eta^{\\mathrm{jet}_{1}, \\mathrm{jet}_{2}} \\in (1.0, 1.5)$, and $\\Delta\\eta^{\\mathrm{jet}_{1}, \\mathrm{jet}_{2}} \\in (1.5, 2.0)$. The result for $2 < p^{\\mathrm{ch}}_{\\mathrm{T}} < 4$ GeV corresponds to $\\mathrm{R^{asym}}$ with $\\Delta\\eta^{\\mathrm{jet}_{1}, \\mathrm{jet}_{2}} \\in (1.0, 1.5)$.",
